## Known holes

{{HOLES}}

- Foursquare's open release is from February 2025 and contains many listings last refreshed 2012–2019. Those are tier C:
  many of them have certainly closed, some certainly still exist. Without a ground survey open data cannot tell.
- Overture is strong on restaurants, cafés and chains, weak on small independent shops (tailors, shoe repair, kiosks).
- Kiosks (περίπτερα): neither Overture nor Foursquare lists most of them; OSM has a few. Real Kifisia has a kiosk at nearly every
  major corner of Kifisias Avenue and Platanos square.
- Upper floors: doctors, lawyers and offices are heavily represented in Foursquare/Overture (Kifisia has hundreds of practices).
  They are marked `streetLevel:false`; they should not take a shop window.
- Greek directories: vrisko.gr category pages are harvested (see Method 4b); xo.gr and 11880.com refuse automated access (HTTP 403)
  and were not used. Google Maps was not scraped.

## What "complete" means here

This file contains every business that at least one open source places inside the play area, de-duplicated, with an honest
statement of how sure we are that it exists today (`tier`, `confidence`, `open`). It is **not** a ground survey: a shop that
opened in 2026 and is in no open dataset is missing, and some tier B entries will have closed. On the main shopping streets
the open sources together are dense, so building tiers A + B there gives streets that match reality far better than OSM alone.

## Scale and position audit (for the commander and the data agent)

{{SCALE}}

Verdict: the world is 1 game unit = 1 real metre. The projection's east–west factor 87716 is 0.034 % smaller than the exact
WGS84 value at Kifisia's latitude (87745.7 m per degree), i.e. 3.4 cm per 100 m — below the 0.1 % threshold, so **no
correction is required**. Every pair over 100 m is within 0.06 %; the only pairs above 0.1 % are 20–60 m pairs where the 0.1 m
coordinate grid of the map JSON (±0.07 m per point) dominates. If the data agent ever wants to remove even that 0.03 %, the exact
constant is `87745.7` (at lat 38.0727); changing it would move the east edge of the map by about 0.4 m — not worth a rebuild.
